A system keeps information about students, lecturers, subjects, and lectures. 
Students can enroll lectures.
Lecturers teach lectures for different subjects.


Additional attributes:
Student: gender, phone_number, email, student code(primary key)
Enrollment: enrollment_status, enrollment_date, student code(primary key), lecture id(foreign key)
Lecture: lecture id(primary key), subject code(foreign key), lecturer id(foreign id), capacity
Lecturer: lecturer id(primary key), subject code(foreign key)
Subject: subject code(primary key)

Relationship:
[Enrolls] - Student->Enrollment->Lecture
    - The Student can enroll in available lectures and lectures can contain many students.
    - One student to one lecture per enrollment process

[Lectures] - Lecturer->Lecture->Subject
    - The Lecturer can teach many lectures
    - A subject can contain many lectures
    - Each lecture is taught by a lecturer and belongs to one subject



Student:
-S_code(primary key)
-F_name
-L_name
-NID
-B_date
-S_address
-S_email
-S_number
-S_gender

Enrollment:
